1. A computer-implemented method for activating charging of an electric vehicle at a charging outlet, the method comprising:

   receiving, by a charging control system associated with the charging outlet, a first charging session identifier from a driver electricity provider associated with a driver of the electric vehicle;

   receiving, by the charging control system, a second charging session identifier from an outlet electricity provider associated with supply of electricity to the charging outlet;

   comparing, by the charging control system, the first charging session identifier with the second charging session identifier;

   determining, based on the comparing, that the first charging session identifier matches the second charging session identifier; and

   in response to determining that the first charging session identifier matches the second charging session identifier, enabling delivery of electrical power from the charging outlet to the electric vehicle for a charging session.

A method for controlling charging of an electric vehicle, comprising:

receiving, by a charging activation device associated with the electric vehicle, a first session identifier from a first service provider associated with an owner or operator of the electric vehicle;

receiving, by the charging activation device, a second session identifier from a second service provider associated with a power outlet or charging supply equipment;

determining, by the charging activation device, that the first session identifier corresponds to the second session identifier; and

in response to determining that the first session identifier corresponds to the second session identifier, enabling delivery of electrical power from the power outlet or charging supply equipment to the electric vehicle to initiate a charging session.

In some embodiments, the charging activation device is disposed in or coupled to the electric vehicle, a charging cable, an adapter, a mobile device, or electric vehicle supply equipment. The first and second session identifiers may be generated in connection with an authorization, reservation, billing, or authentication process and may be received via wireless, wired, short-range, cellular, internet-based, or vehicle-to-infrastructure communication. Enabling delivery of electrical power may include closing a relay, authorizing a control pilot signal, transmitting an activation command, unlocking a connector, or otherwise permitting current flow for charging the electric vehicle.
